 \section{Introduction}\label{sec:intro}
-Formal verification services check streams of program and proof candidates against formal specifications. Proof-generation systems submit related attempts that share libraries, declarations and accepted context. Services use proof assistants to construct and check proof terms, or verifiers to translate program obligations into requests to satisfiability modulo theories (SMT) solvers. Community tools for Lean~\cite{lean4} expose persistent environments for these workloads~\cite{repl}.
+Formal verification services check streams of program and proof candidates against formal specifications. Proof-generation systems submit related attempts that share libraries, declarations and accepted context. Services check these attempts with proof assistants that construct and check proof terms, or with verifiers that translate program obligations into requests to satisfiability modulo theories (SMT) solvers. Community tools for Lean~\cite{lean4} expose persistent environments for these workloads~\cite{repl}.
 
-Serving independent attempts trades repeated preparation against shared execution. A separate verifier for each candidate repeats imports and parsing and replicates resident objects. Retained workers and shared logical environments avoid that repetition, but resource growth, contention and cancellation depend on worker isolation. Concurrent attempts against one imported Lean context illustrate the tradeoff: they need the same context and independent lifetimes. Cancelling one attempt must release its speculative work without ending the others.
+Serving independent attempts requires balancing repeated preparation with shared execution. A separate verifier for each candidate repeats imports and parsing and replicates resident objects. Retained workers and shared logical environments avoid that repetition, but their resource growth, contention and cancellation behavior depend on worker isolation. For example, concurrent attempts against one imported Lean context need the same context but have independent lifetimes. Cancelling one attempt must release its speculative work without ending the others.
 
 This tradeoff depends on native execution history beyond visible formulas or declarations. Z3's combined solver can select a different solving path after an additional scope~\cite{z3api}, and earlier requests can alter heuristics and resource counters. A proof assistant likewise retains elaborator state and mutable runtime extensions beyond its immutable declaration environment~\cite{lean4,repl}. Reconstructing a logically equivalent context therefore requires a separate argument for observable verification behavior.
 
-Established reuse recovers preparation but leaves the value of independent native execution at matched resources unresolved. Result caches avoid repeating completed work~\cite{boogieCache}, while the community read--eval--print loop (REPL) supports persistent environments, backtracking and pickling~\cite{repl}. Recent Lean snapshotting retains elaborated proof state across parallel tactic branches~\cite{leanSnapshot}, and stock Lean saves incremental elaboration snapshots between invocations~\cite{leanIncremental}. Bounded warm services reuse environment roots and retire workers~\cite{kimina,kiminaPaper}. Against these native-reuse baselines, the matched comparison must establish whether separating preparation from candidate execution history improves complete verification, cancellation and total memory across service processes.
+Established reuse recovers preparation but leaves the value of independent native execution at matched resources unresolved. Result caches avoid repeating completed work~\cite{boogieCache}, while the community read--eval--print loop (REPL) supports persistent environments, backtracking and pickling~\cite{repl}. Recent Lean snapshotting retains elaborated proof state across parallel tactic branches~\cite{leanSnapshot}, and stock Lean saves incremental elaboration snapshots between invocations~\cite{leanIncremental}. Bounded warm services reuse environment roots and retire workers~\cite{kimina,kiminaPaper}. Axle also serves preloaded Lean contexts in separate request processes~\cite{axle}. Against these native-reuse baselines, the matched comparison must establish whether separating preparation from candidate execution history improves complete verification, cancellation and total memory across service processes.
 
 We argue that reusable verification state should retain preparation while separating each candidate's execution history and lifetime. A context is prepared before candidate evaluation, and that native state remains available to independent attempts. Each candidate inherits the prepared state, so other candidates neither supply its solver history nor extend its lifetime. The value of this separation depends on context preparation cost, branch creation cost and the pages that each candidate modifies.
 
 Realizing this separation requires runtime safety, faithful resource handling and bounded memory. A branch boundary must be quiescent and safe for the verifier runtime. Native configuration and resource accounting must remain faithful when process creation changes timers or descriptors~\cite{fork}. Preparation sharing must improve service capacity within a memory budget that bounds retained states. Together, these requirements connect compatibility to the service's resource frontier, the achievable combinations of latency, throughput and memory use at matched CPU capacity and memory limits.
 
